  "name": null,
  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true when testing the stability of Euler's method on the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),\\,y(0)=\\frac{7}{3},\\,x\\ge 0,\\,\\lambda =\\frac{11}{5},$ and step size $Δx?$  \n\nI. The update formula can be written as ${y}_{n+1}={(1-\\frac{11}{5}Δx)}^{n}{y}_{n}.$\n\nII. The method is stable for $|1-\\frac{11}{5}Δx|<1.$\n\nIII. The method is **unstable** for step size $Δx=0.3.$\n\nIV. The method is **unstable** for step size $Δx=1.$",
